course: dictionary
lesson: 15008
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so the context tells you which meaning to use. First ask what kind of word it is: a noun names a thing, and a verb is an action word.
explain: «The squirrels store nuts in their winter reserves.» Reserves are supplies kept for later. The clue is winter: the squirrels are saving food for the cold months.
explain: «The team's reserves ran on when a player was hurt.» Here reserves are extra players who wait on the bench, ready to join in if needed.
explain: «She reserves a table for six at the café.» Now reserves is a verb, an action word. She books the table, so it is kept for her.
fact: «Reserves» can be a noun (more than one reserve) or a verb (to reserve means to book or keep something).
fact: Reserves are supplies kept for later or for an emergency, like «food reserves» or «energy reserves».
fact: In sport, reserves are substitutes who sit on the bench and come on if needed.
fact: A «nature reserve» is land protected for wild animals and plants.
fact: Check the context: try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
exercise: «The farmer kept grain in reserves for the cold months.» What are the reserves? | *Supplies kept for later | Animals that live in the wild | Players who wait on the bench | Dinners cooked in a pot
exercise: «The team's reserves ran on when a player was hurt.» What does reserves mean here? | Wild land kept safe | Things that are broken | Supplies of food | *Extra players who come on if needed
exercise: «Sam reserves a seat on the bus.» Reserves is a verb here. What does it mean? | *Books it so it is kept for him | Throws it away | Paints it blue | Sits down on it
test: «The wildlife reserve is home to rare birds.» What kind of reserve is this? | Extra players on a team | *Protected land for wild animals and plants | Money saved in a bank | A list of rules
test: «Bears eat a lot in summer and build fat reserves for winter.» What are fat reserves? | Thick paint for walls | Fat that has been spilled | Soft pillows for sleeping | *Stored energy kept for a hard time
exam: «Mum reserves two tickets for the show.» Reserves is a verb here. What does it mean? | *To keep and book something for later | To paint a picture | To throw something away | To sell something at a shop
